{"case_id":"C108","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":98,"change_types":["new input-format support","attack-surface expansion","new pixel-conversion paths"],"affected_functions":["decoder.decode_image_config?","wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__prepare","wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__prepare__bgra_nonpremul","wuffs_base__composite_premul_nonpremul_u32_axxx"],"reason":"The commit materially expands BMP decoding to accept BITMAPINFOHEADER sizes 40 and 108 in addition to 124, and adds 32-bpp BGRA_NONPREMUL decoding plus new swizzler/compositing paths. The supplied harnesses exercise only GIF and zlib entry points, so they do not provide input control over BMP headers, masks, compression normalization, or 32-bpp pixel data. The generic build loop does not establish that a BMP target exists because no BMP harness is supplied.","evidence":["`gif_fuzzer.c` initializes `wuffs_gif__decoder` and invokes only GIF decode methods.","`zlib_fuzzer.c` initializes `wuffs_zlib__decoder` and invokes only `wuffs_zlib__decoder__transform_io`.","`decoder.decode_image_config?` now accepts `bitmap_info_len` values 40, 108, and 124, whereas it previously accepted only 124.","BMP decoding now accepts `bits_per_pixel == 32` and selects `BGRA_NONPREMUL` (`repr: 0x4500_8888`).","The change parses `mask_r`, `mask_g`, `mask_b`, and `mask_a`, and conditionally converts BITFIELDS compression value 3 to uncompressed handling.","`wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__prepare` gains a `BGRA_NONPREMUL` branch with new SRC and SRC_OVER conversion implementations."],"recommended_action":"Add or update a BMP fuzz target to drive the full image-config, frame-config, and frame-decode path with version 3/4/5 headers, 32-bpp data, explicit channel masks, and relevant destination pixel formats/blend modes."}
